invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: a host object stops packaging ghash_hw.c, so it carries aes_hw.c
  and a gcm.c that calls two GHASH entries no source in the object
  defines. A linker would refuse the test binaries, but a linker is not
  the gate: it names a missing symbol, not the build that lost its
  source, and a firmware tree that copies the source list from here would
  meet the error in its own build. The lint reads the packaged source
  list per build, and its host rows require the four sources of the AES
  instructions.

--- old
AES_HW_SRCS := aes_hw.c ghash_hw.c gcm_hw.c gcm_vaes.c
--- new
AES_HW_SRCS := aes_hw.c gcm_hw.c gcm_vaes.c
